# Build output and local caches, none of which a container build needs.
#
# The context for this repository is dominated by things `go build` regenerates: bin/ holds five
# cross-compiled binaries from `just cross` (48 MB measured), .cache/ holds the race binary and
# the synthetic fixture (16 MB), and .git/ is 21 MB. Without this file every `docker build`
# uploads all of it before the first byte of source is copied.
bin/
.cache/

# Model files are gigabytes and are never part of the image -- see the Dockerfile's note on
# mounting a checkpoint instead.
*.gguf
models/

# Test and profile artifacts.
*.test
*.out
*.prof
coverage.*

# Tool caches and editor state.
.rumdl_cache/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# The git directory itself. The Dockerfile does not read it: version metadata comes from
# --build-arg, because a build context has no guarantee of a usable .git and stamping a wrong
# commit hash is worse than stamping none.
.git/
.github/

# Repository documentation and tooling, which the binary does not embed.
docs/
scripts/
CONTRIBUTING.md
USAGE-VALIDATION.md
